        'Insertion sort, Timsort, Linear/Binary/Interpolation/Jump search, Hashing, and Algorithm Selection',
        '# Data Structures and Algorithms (DSA)\n\n## Beginner: Linear Search & Insertion Sort\nLinear search checks elements one-by-one in O(n) time and O(1) space on unsorted data. Insertion Sort builds a sorted array key-by-key in O(n^2) worst case and O(n) best-case time.\n\n## Intermediate: Binary Search & Timsort\nBinary Search requires sorted arrays, halving range in O(log n) time using overflow-safe `mid = low + (high - low) // 2`. Python `sorted()` uses Timsort (hybrid Insertion + Merge Sort) with O(n log n) worst-case. Hash sets/dicts provide average O(1) lookups.\n\n## Advanced & Experienced Engineer: Search Selection Matrix\n- Linear Search: Unsorted data, single lookup.\n- Binary Search: Sorted data, repeated queries.\n- Interpolation Search: O(log log n) best case on uniformly distributed sorted keys.\n- Exponential Search: O(log n) on bounded/unbounded arrays.\n- Multi-query break-even: Sorting once O(n log n) + Q binary searches beats Q linear scans when Q > log n.',
