        'Semantic HTML5, CSS Box Model, Display types, Positioning, Viewports, and Media Queries',
        '# Front-End Web Development: HTML and CSS\n\n## Beginner: HTML5 Structure & Semantic Layout\nHTML documents begin with `<!DOCTYPE html>`. `<html>` holds `<head>` metadata and `<body>` UI. Semantic tags: `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<footer>`. Rule: Exactly one `<h1>` per page.\n\n## Intermediate: CSS Box Model & Viewport\nBox Model: Content, Padding, Border, Margin. Use `box-sizing: border-box` to include padding/border in declared width. Viewport meta: `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">`. Positioning: `static`, `relative`, `absolute`, `fixed`, `sticky`.\n\n## Advanced & Experienced Engineer: Responsive Grid & Flexbox\nUse Flexbox for 1D layouts and CSS Grid for 2D layouts. Responsive media queries `@media (min-width: 768px)` create fluid mobile-first layouts.',
