        'JS Engine, DOM Selection, Hoisting, Arrow Functions, Events, Event Delegation, Async, and Event Loop',
        '# Front-End Web Development: JavaScript\n\n## Beginner: JS Fundamentals & DOM\nBrowser engines (V8) execute JS. `var` is function-scoped; `let` and `const` are block-scoped. DOM Selection: `getElementById`, `querySelector`, `querySelectorAll`. Use `textContent` for safe text injection (prevents XSS).\n\n## Intermediate: Hoisting & Event Delegation\nFunction declarations are fully hoisted; function expressions and arrow functions are not. Event delegation attaches a single event listener to a parent container, using `event.target` to handle child triggers efficiently.\n\n## Advanced & Experienced Engineer: Event Loop Architecture\nSingle-threaded model: Call Stack -> Microtask Queue (Promises / async-await) -> Macrotask Queue (setTimeout / setInterval). Event loop drains all microtasks before processing macrotasks.',
