        '# Databases and SQL\n\n## Beginner: SQL Sub-Languages & Constraints\nDDL (`CREATE TABLE`), DML (`INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`), DQL (`SELECT`). Constraints: PRIMARY KEY, FOREIGN KEY, NOT NULL, UNIQUE, DEFAULT, CHECK.\n\n## Intermediate: WHERE Safety & SQL Joins\nAlways include `WHERE` on `UPDATE` and `DELETE` to avoid mutating all rows. DELETE removes matching rows; TRUNCATE clears table keeping structure; DROP deletes table entirely. Joins: INNER, LEFT, RIGHT, FULL.\n\n## Advanced & Experienced Engineer: Logical Execution Order & GROUP BY vs HAVING\nSQL Execution Order: 1. FROM/JOIN 2. WHERE 3. GROUP BY 4. HAVING 5. SELECT 6. ORDER BY 7. LIMIT. `WHERE` filters rows before aggregation; `HAVING` filters aggregated groups after `GROUP BY`.',
